  "adaptations": [
    "Oracle bloom storage format is rgba16float to exercise the required linear HDR graph rather than native rgba8unorm clipping.",
    "Oracle DoF replaces implicit textureSample with textureSampleLevel(..., 0) for compute-stage validation; its formula and kernels are unchanged.",
    "AO inputs are converted from normalized linear depth/world normals to native linear view depth/packed view normals. Frame index is fixed to zero for deterministic sampling.",
    "Lens oracle receives display-encoded colors; browser defers the transfer to the final output.",
    "Native bloom blur needs an explicit f32 cast on its i32 offsets under current WGSL validation.",
    "Native bloom composite uniform uses WGSL-required 32-byte allocation (vec3 alignment).",
    "Denoise oracle reads normalized linear depth from r32float instead of a depth attachment; texture declaration and .r loads are the only shader changes. Browser additionally stops at object, normal and albedo boundaries.",
    "TAA comparison uses stationary zero-jitter inputs. Browser adds ID/previous-depth rejection and resolves onto the unjittered pixel grid.",
    "Realtime motion blur uses bounded depth-aware velocity sampling; the historical terrain shutter accumulator is retained as a provenance anchor. Offline temporal shutter sampling remains available via W06."
  ],
  "threshold": {
    "ssim": 0.98,
    "negativeControlRequired": true
  }
}
